update progressnote set description ='<p>Supervision with Virginia &amp; Tanesha.</p><p>Crisis regarding Larnell Perry;  September 14, 2023. The request has been for a VPA. Received daniels.</p><p>Family Support Worker, Bright arrived to the home first. Larnell came out of his room eating a rice krispy treat. Larnell wanted to get some other snack ( his sisters Twixt candy). Child became upset, ran out of the house. Child went through doggy door. Child came back into the home as his mother pursued him. Larnell continued to tantrum in his room. Child''s mother opened his bedroom door. Child became aggressive toward his mother, hitting her and throwing things. FSW called 911 and the Crisis Response.  Case Work Specialist, Virginia arrived during the fray. Worker tried to calm Larnell done. Larnell escalated by attempting to throw a heavy duty cake mixer toward the worker. Child tried to bite Virginia as he had his teeth on worker''s harm, but child''s mother redirected Larnell to stop. Larnell reportedly kicked worker. Worker reported that she is fine.</p><p>Child cursed Virginia, calling her bitch. Reportedly, nine police (male) and one woman (1) arrived at the home. </p><p> Child is described as very petite. Child''s eyes were dilated and his affect was angry. Larnell was not able to de escalate so the police put the Larnell in handcuffs. Larnell reportedly kicked the police car so hard resulting in a dent in the police car. Child  was transported to Children''s Hospital ( one police drive and two police were in the back seat with child, Larnell. ) Two paramedics were present also.</p><p>Worker spoke to Ms. Perry today and physician, Dr. Shot. Dr.Shot, described mental state as a baseline condition (chronic). Due to chronic behavior: diagnosis: ADHD, PTSD, Autism and four other diagnosis; Children''s Hospital Dr. Shot reported the hospital cannot treat Larnel as he needs long term care. Children''s Hospital reported that Larnell would be discharged;  and child needed to go to John Hopkins Hospital, Kennedy Krieger or Sheppard Pratt. Moreover, Children''s  Hospital does not transport to another hospital. Reportedly, Ms. Perry has to pick up her child and transport to John Hopkins, Kennedy Krieger and Sheppard Pratt.  Worker was informed that if Ms. Perry does not pick up her son at discharge, Children''s Hospital will file a CPS report for neglect.</p><p>It must be noted: ( FSW reported) On this past  Saturday, Larnell went to  the Cheesecake Factory with his mother and his mother''s boyfriend, Jeff. There were no ribs on the menu so Larnell became anger. Larnell attempted to stab Jeff in the hand). Mother took child out of the restaurant, was able to calm  Larnell done. Larnell was able to return to the restaurant. </p><p>Assessment: Larnell has been assaultive to his mother. He is a  threat to himself, his sister and his mother.</p><p>Status of VPA; (Amorelle is the FAR unit worker) Denials for RTCl is in CJAMS).</p><p>SCACC-Denied. Child is violet and a runner.</p><p>Acacia- denial.</p><p>Plan: Explore Limited Custody, Judge to order child to enter state hospital pending seeking out of state RTC., Or mother will revisit allowing her sister to place the child in the state she resides in (Pennsylvania). </p>',
updatedby ='CDM-34309',updatedon =now() where progressnoteid = '9e5379a8-e6bd-49c1-aeb0-5be605328dbb' and witsid ='11408304' and activeflag =1;

